  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Praluent (alirocumab) / Repatha (evolocumab) PCSK9 inhibitor Criteria Version 3; Original 4/29/2016; Updated 4/17/2026; Effective 6/1/2026.",
    "Both products share approval and denial criteria. Closed indication attests diagnosis or calculated risk and the primary hypercholesterolemia pre-treatment baseline LDL-C threshold.",
    "FDA age: primary hypercholesterolemia and increased MACE risk are adult indications. Familial uses the permissive HeFH floor: Praluent \u22658 years; Repatha \u226510 years. Praluent HoFH is adult-only and requires manual review because familial subtype is not collected; Repatha HeFH and HoFH are labeled for age \u226510 years.",
    "LDL targets are ASCVD <70 mg/dL and non-ASCVD <100 mg/dL. Either documented failed-target option is accepted across indications: calculated ASCVD risk does not establish ASCVD disease, and familial/primary hypercholesterolemia may coexist with ASCVD. Denial for at/below goal before initiation is represented by the failing LDL option.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 1 year.",
    "Quantity (notes only): Praluent 150 mg every 14 days; Repatha ASCVD/HeFH 140 mg every 14 days or 420 mg every 28 days; Repatha HoFH 420 mg every 14 days. Product/subtype dosing requires manual review; max_units is null.",
    "Caution (notes only): hypersensitivity reactions, including angioedema, have occurred.",
    "PDL status unknown. Leqvio is linked as an alternative, not concurrent therapy.",
    "Remains partial: submitted chart notes/labs, diagnosis, treatment history and baseline lipids are attestations; evidence verification, Praluent HoFH adult-only labeling, duration, reauthorization, dosing, quantity and cautions require manual review."
  ],
  "max_units": null,
